  "decision": "map_front",
  "rationale": "Round 2 gained +45.3% HV (354.2) and the front is still expanding, but it covers only part of the objectives' ranges: accuracy_bits spans 12..21.9 while the registry (data_width up to 28, output LSB 2^-(W-2)) permits roughly 26 bits, and power_index spans only 1.98..6.34 against an HV reference of 40. All 10 shown Pareto points are pipelined_m (pipelined's best feasible power_index is 3.47), and the feasible pipelined_m ranges already seen (data_width 16..26, n_iter 14..30, angle_guard -2..3, frac_guard 0..4, m 2..3) are wider than what the front samples, so the high-accuracy tail (21.9..~26 bits) and the low-power corner near the 2^-12 constraint are under-mapped. With 80 evals left and 2 rounds, spending this round on NSGA-II over the full ranges of the two on-front families (pipelined, pipelined_m), seeded with the current 16-design front, is the best way to cover the whole trade-off curve before the reserved end-of-run mapping. No family change is needed (iterative/unrolled_k cannot reach the 50 MSPS constraint), and the constraints are clearly reachable (best max_abs_err 2.49e-07, best throughput 180 MSPS), so infeasible/stop are not warranted.",
  "next_plan": null
}
